211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Our system is built on a large VLM-based agent framework that operates entirely on-device. Within this framework, several offline specialized agent models work independently to analyze different aspects of the input IC. These include a pin-segmentation and counting model, a potential surface-defect detection model, and a dimensional-mask extraction model that verifies the physical geometry of the IC.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (All these agent outputs are then passed to the VLM, along with the OEM-parsed datasheet information. This datasheet module has already extracted the expected pin count, package dimensions, and other critical specifications directly from the manufacturer's document, ensuring a trusted reference baseline for comparison.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (By combining the multimodal agent inferences with the verified datasheet specifications, the VLM generates a final confidence score indicating how confidently the system believes the IC is genuine. This structured flow ensures a robust, explainable, and high-accuracy IC authenticity assessment.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
